B -- IS THE SIGN OF psi PREDICTABLE ON THE REAL DATA?
    Ljung-Box(10) on sign(psi_j,t): the sign process is BOUNDED, so the
    chi^2(10) calibration is valid where it was not for psi itself.
    chi^2(10) 95% = 18.31.  Contrast with ||psi||^2, which should and does
    show dependence -- magnitude clusters, and that is not the issue.
